# Per-instance credentials for the BoxStats containers in config.json. A box names the
# VARIABLE holding its credential, never the credential itself — "secret": "ADGUARD_MAIN"
# is read from DASHBOARD_SECRET_ADGUARD_MAIN, verbatim: no uppercasing and no punctuation
# folding, so a lowercase name reads a lowercase variable. One variable per instance, so
# two boxes can have two logins.
#
# Named here but left unset (or empty) is an ABSENCE, not a failure: that box is skipped,
# warned about once in the server log, and nobody is toasted.
#
# What the value is, per provider:
#   adguard      username:password   (sent as HTTP Basic; the first colon splits it)
#   pihole5      the API token from Settings -> API / Web interface
#   pihole6      the web interface password
#   uptime-kuma  nothing — a public status page needs no secret, so omit "secret" entirely
DASHBOARD_SECRET_ADGUARD_MAIN=

# Where config.json lives. Resolved from the server's working directory at startup, so
# prefer an absolute path for anything but a dev run.
# DASHBOARD_CONFIG=config.json

# Set this and /admin becomes a config editor, guarded by this one shared secret. Unset,
# the whole admin area returns 404 rather than 401 — a feature that is switched off must
# not advertise that it exists. Rotating it signs everyone out; that is the entire
# revocation mechanism. Generate one with:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
DASHBOARD_ADMIN_TOKEN=
